quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  3,109,"To Allah belongs all that is in the heavens and on the earth. And to Allah, all matters will be returned."
  3,110,"You are the best nation (ever) brought forth for (the guidance of) humankind: you enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong and believe in Allah. And if the People of the Book had believed, it would have certainly been better for them. Few of them are (true) believers, and most of them are evil-doers."
  3,111,"They will never do you much harm except hurting a little. If they fight you, they will turn their backs (to flee) and will not be helped."
  3,112,They will be stricken with disgrace wherever confronted unless (they are provided asylum) under some covenant from Allah or the people. They have incurred Allah’s wrath and have been subjected to poverty. That is because they would persistently disbelieve in Allah’s revelations and kill the prophets wrongly. That is because they acted rebelliously and used to commit transgression.
  3,113,Yet they are not all alike. Among the People of the Book is an upright group; they recite Allah’s revelations during night hours while remaining in prostration (before their Lord).
  3,114,"They believe in Allah and the Last Day, enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong and are prompt in (performing) good deeds. And they are among the righteous."
  3,115,"And whatever good they do, they will never be denied (the just reward of it). And Allah is All-Knowing of the God-conscious."
